{
  "Picks one item from a list. The field shows the chosen item; the list opens below it with the keyboard or a press, can be searched, grouped and drawn your way, and stays fast with thousands of items.": "",
  "Objects of your own are read through `textField` and `valueField` (a name or a function); `groupField` puts options under headers, `enabledField` keeps some from being chosen, and a template draws an option your way.": "",
  "Search and long lists": "",
  "`searchEnabled` puts a search box at the top of the list. A long list draws only the rows in view: this one has 5,000 orders.": "",
  "Items that change": "",
  "`items` given as a function is followed: a new list shows at once. Your items may be plain or reactive; the drop-down reads them as they are, so after changing them in place, call `refresh()`: the open list and the field show the change.": "",
  "Open the list on the chosen option (Home / End: on the first / last).": "",
  "Open the list on the next option starting with it; letters typed quickly search together.": "",
  "Move the highlight; options that cannot be chosen are skipped.": "",
  "Choose the highlighted option and close.": "",
  "Choose the highlighted option and go on to the next field.": "",
  "Close without choosing; with `clearButton` and the list closed, empty the value.": "",
  "Focus the field.": "",
  "The APG select-only combobox: the field is `role=\"combobox\"` with `aria-haspopup=\"listbox\"`, `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`; focus stays on it.": "",
  "`aria-activedescendant` names the highlighted option; options are `role=\"option\"` with `aria-selected`, disabled ones `aria-disabled`.": "",
  "Only the rows in view are drawn; each option says where it is with `aria-posinset` and `aria-setsize`.": "",
  "The search box controls the list and names the highlighted option the same way.": "",
  "While the value's item is asked for, the combobox is `aria-busy` and its text says \"Loading…\" to screen readers; a key the source does not have carries the reason as its title.": "",
  "The search box, the clear button, the empty list text, the wait (`loading`) and the reason a key is marked (`notInList`, `loadFailed`) come from `uiLocale.strings`.": "",
  "Added to the field. `data-open` while the list is open, `data-loading` while the value's item is asked for; the field attributes of TextBox.": "",
  "The combobox, the chosen text (`data-placeholder` when empty, `data-missing` for a key the source does not have), the arrow.": "",
  "The spinner in the arrow's place while the value's item is asked for.": "",
  "The popup and its search box.": "",
  "The list (shared), its options (`data-active`, `data-selected`) and group headers.": "",
  "The field, as for TextBox.": "",
  "Units: the chosen text (`placeholder`, `missing`, `disabled`), the arrow (`open`, `disabled`), the ring that turns while the value's item is asked for and the shape a language may draw instead (with the spinner's shapes and timing).": "",
  "The options: their row height, and the item unit in each state (`hover`, `pressed`, `active`, `selected`, `selected-hover`, `selected-pressed`, `disabled`, `next`, `select-all`).": "",
  "Units: the bar on the chosen option (`multiple`), the check of a list of several choices and its mark, an icon, the text.": "",
  "Units: the list (its space and most height), a group, group headers, the line under \"Select all\", the empty text.": "",
  "The value of the chosen item. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "Plain values, `DropDownItem`s (`{ value, text, icon?, group?, enabled? }`) or objects of your own. A function is followed; items changed in place show after `refresh()`.": "",
  "Items from the data layer, loaded where the list is scrolled to and searched on its `searchFields`. Wins over `items`. A value on no loaded page is asked for by key; meanwhile the field waits (see Lookup).": "",
  "The value's text while its item is asked for from `dataSource`, shown at once instead of waiting (a record that carries the name: `valueText={() => order.customerName}`).": "",
  "`250` with a data source, else `0`": "",
  "Milliseconds between the last key in the search box and the search.": "",
  "A property name or a function `(item) => …`. Without `valueField` an object with a `value` gives that, anything else is its own value.": "",
  "An icon per option; options with the same group follow each other under its name; options that cannot be chosen.": "",
  "A search box at the top of the list.": "",
  "How the search matches the option text.": "",
  "A button that empties the value; Escape does the same while the list is closed.": "",
  "Draws an option / the chosen item yourself.": "",
  "The item whose value is the value.": "",
  "Opens the list; `search` starts the search box with that text. `false` when disabled, read-only, or while the value's item is asked for.": "",
  "Closes it; focus goes back to the field.": "",
  "Your items may be plain or reactive; the drop-down reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. The field's text and the open list follow.": "",
  "The list closed: `'escape'`, `'outside'`, `'focus'` or `'code'` (also after a choice).": "",
  "The list is a shared part, `OptionList`, exported for combo boxes, list boxes and your own controls.": ""
}
